    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Urgent surgical oncology (breast) consultation for a biopsy-proven, node-positive breast cancer, to plan the operation and the axilla. Guideline: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Same-week diagnostic mammography and ultrasound of both breasts and both axillae, and ultrasound-guided core biopsy of the mass and the abnormal node with ER, PR, and HER2 testing. Guideline: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Genetic counseling and germline multigene panel testing (including BRCA2, BRCA1, PALB2, CHEK2, and ATM), as for every man with breast cancer, with a letter for relatives if a variant is found. Guideline: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); Bedrosian I, et al. Germline Testing in Patients With Breast Cancer: ASCO-Society of Surgical Oncology Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2024;42(5):584-604 (2024) [S]</item><item>Mastectomy with axillary lymph node dissection, then shoulder exercises and lymphedema risk reduction with arm measurements at each visit. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Runowicz CD, et al. American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016) [S]</item><item>Adjuvant chemotherapy given by medical oncology (doxorubicin and cyclophosphamide every three weeks for four cycles, then weekly paclitaxel for twelve weeks, about six months), after a baseline echocardiogram, hepatitis B screening, vaccines, and a dental review; radiation oncology review of post-mastectomy radiation after chemotherapy. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Armenian SH, et al. Prevention and Monitoring of Cardiac Dysfunction in Survivors of Adult Cancers: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2017;35(8):893-911 (2017); Hwang JP, et al. Hepatitis B Virus Screening and Management for Patients With Cancer Prior to Therapy: ASCO Provisional Clinical Opinion Update. J Clin Oncol 2020 (2020) [S]</item><item>Tamoxifen after chemotherapy for at least five years, the first-choice endocrine therapy for men, with venous thromboembolism, mood, hot flash, sexual side effect, and adherence checks at every visit. Guideline: Hassett MJ, et al. Management of Male Breast Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2020;38(16):1849-1863 (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Distress screening at each visit, plain information that men get breast cancer, confidential handling of his diagnosis at work, and the offer of a peer-support group for men with breast cancer. Guideline: Runowicz CD, et al. American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

